   $qq$On a number line, $p = -3.75$ and $q = -5.2$. The value of $p - q$ tells how far and in which direction $p$ is from $q$. What is $p - q$?$qq$, $q$[{"text":"$-8.95$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-the-negative-as-if-positive"},{"text":"$8.95$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-signs-and-added"},{"text":"$-1.45$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-sign-on-result"},{"text":"$1.45$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$1.45$$q$, $qq$Subtracting a negative is adding its opposite: $-3.75 - (-5.2) = -3.75 + 5.2 = 1.45$. The positive result means $p$ is $1.45$ units to the right of $q$. The choice $-8.95$ treats $-(-5.2)$ as $-5.2$.$qq$, 'draft', null)
